{"challenges":[{"attack":"Could v1 still control because v2 is later but not otherwise authoritative?","claim_id":"current-time","outcome":"survives","result":"The supplied v2 text expressly says, “This amendment replaces the time in v1.” Thus, within these records, the v1 time is superseded." ,"tool_ids":[]}],"checks":[{"basis_reasoning":"This is a source attribution: schedule-original contains the quoted statement. It establishes what that supplied record says, not the independent truth or authority of the record.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"original-time","reasoning":"The cited source text states that draft schedule v1 records the project review for Thursday at 09:30 local time.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"This is a source attribution: schedule-amendment contains the quoted statement. It establishes the amendment's stated content, not independently its authenticity or authority.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"amendment-time","reasoning":"The cited source text says the review moved to Thursday at 10:00 local time and that the amendment replaces the time in v1.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"The derivation is supported by the source-attributed amendment statement and its explicit replacement language; no unstated priority rule is needed among these two records.","basis_verdict":"applicable","checked_step_ids":["step-current-time"],"claim_id":"current-time","reasoning":"Step-current-time correctly distinguishes the historical v1 entry from the instruction in v2: v2 specifies 10:00 local time and explicitly replaces v1's time. Therefore the records support Thursday at 10:00 local time as the current instruction.","verdict":"supported"}],"missing_evidence":[],"recommended_action":"finish","tool_requests":[]}
